 Links - The Challenge of Golf Enhanced 2.0b (25.11.2026)
 Original install: StingRay. Version 2.0b: Vesuri.

 This install applies to "LINKS - The Challenge of Golf © 1992 Access.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad to be in the path.
 This program can be found in the WHDLoad package.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed game requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1.0 MB OtherMem(+3.1 MB for preload)
 It can be quit by pressing F10 (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate message.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.


 Features:
 ---------
 - Full load from HD
 - 2 versions supported (v1.50 and v1.53)
 - Course selection bug fixed, now all courses are displayed (see below)
 - Bountiful and Firestone course disks supported
 - Cache stuff disabled
 - Intro can be skipped with CUSTOM1
 - Manual included
 - NewIcon (created by me)
 - Source code included as usual
 - Quit option that works on 68000 machines (default key is 'F10')

 Here's the patch for one of the most resource hungry golf games on the
 Amiga ever. Game has been coded in assembly but the code could have been
 a lot faster, it's not very optimised. 


 Update 28-Apr-2013
 ------------------
 
 Today I added support for the course disks, what I thought would be a
 quick update of the install script turned out to be a bugfixing session
 because the course disk support apparently was never tested with more
 than one course. The game destroyed the FIB (FileInfoBlock) while trying
 to read the course name so only 1 course would be displayed in the
 course selection screen. Pretty lame bug in my opinion which is now
 fixed, all courses are now displayed and can be selected!

 Supported are the Firestone and Bountiful course disks, as far as I know
 there are no other course disks available. You can install them using
 the install package.
 In case you have a different course disk just copy the course
 (any file with .crs extension) to the course directory and the game
 will use it. 
 
 There also is a so called "v2.0" version of the game, it's the Kixx XL
 budget release and a horribly hacked 1.53 version (file names changed
 in a more than pathetic way to make the game run from disk), I will
 NOT support this, please use the original v1.53 version.


 That about wraps it up, enjoy the game!
 Sting, 28-Apr-2013



